{
  "schema": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Vector file of FN-46 (one meaning per field): the same text typed into a field and typed or pasted into the grid must give the same result.",
    "How it was derived: each expectation was produced by running TODAY's reading functions of the editor on the text, under Node, and then compared with the two tables of FN-46 in the specification (every row of the second table agrees).",
    "Readers: q, beta and alpha_k use parseProbability / parseNumberText (range 0 to 1); lambda and mu use numberParser(0) over parseNumber (at least 0); T and tau use numberParser(0, exclusive) over parseNumber (above 0).",
    "A value is in stored units: lambda and mu per hour (lambda read with the header unit /h), T and tau in hours; -0 is stored as 0.",
    "Blank text: typed into lambda, T, tau or mu it clears the field (ok, value null); typed into q, beta or alpha_k it is refused; pasted into the grid, an empty (or spaces-only) cell leaves the cell unchanged (FN-50) and is not read at all.",
    "Numeric values are compared with a relative tolerance of 1e-12."
  ],
  "columns": ["q", "lambda", "T", "tau", "mu", "beta", "alpha_k"],
  "ranges": {
    "q": "[0, 1]", "lambda": "[0, inf)", "T": "(0, inf)", "tau": "(0, inf)", "mu": "[0, inf)", "beta": "[0, 1]", "alpha_k": "[0, 1]"
  },
  "lambda_units": {"h": 1, "y": 8760, "FIT": 1e9},
